      Arabic is the default locale set: the app was Arabic-first before it was
      anything else, and until the language switch lands (P1) these values are
      what every device sees. P1 moves this file to values-ar/ and puts the
      English translation here; call sites do not change.

      Placeholders: %1$s is always a pre-formatted number string (already
      thousands-separated and, when the user asks for it, in Arabic-Indic
      digits) — never a raw integer, so no %d appears in this file.
